# EXPORT_KT_S9H_v1: the C2-a thresholds and per-piece slacks of kt_s9h_v1_3_2 (sweep), for P2-12 and P2-16; format S4U_KV_v1 ("KEY = value"; # lines are comments). Piece lines: N<N>_P<index> = jlo jhi | name dmin slack_lo ; ... per kind and joint class.
FORMAT = S4U_KV_v1
RECORD = EXPORT_KT_S9H_v1
PRODUCER = pk07
CODE = pk07/kt_s9h_v1_3_2.py:723a1945
RUN = sweep
RUN_VERDICT = VALID
EXPORT_STATUS = CERTIFIED
COVERAGE_RULE = P2-11 covers a pair of kind K (FLIP, SAME, MIXED) at N iff both of its end exponents are >= DH_N<N>_<K>, and P2-14's joint kind covers the overlapping pairs D3, D4, D4M at N iff both end exponents of the window are >= DH_N<N>_OVERLAP; P2-12 covers the rest at n >= 6 and P2-13 covers n <= 5
END_EXPONENT_RULE = columns are counted 1..n from each end, 1 at the end column; a vertical edge at column j from that end has end exponent d = j - 2 there, so an end column has d = -1 (S8's convention, SPEC_S8_CERT_v1 c0f95398 sect. 1); a t or bb edge takes its column nearer that end; a joint window takes its outer column on each side; e = R_w rho1^d with d the smaller of the two end exponents. Example: in an n = 6 strip a vertical on column 1 or column 6 has d = -1, and a t edge on columns 2-3 has d_L = 0 and d_R = 2
CLAIM_RULE = DH_N<N>_<K> is the smallest d at which the kind's k = 0 slack is certainly > 0 on every piece at d and at every larger d (checked for d <= DH_MAX; larger d follow, the slack being nonincreasing in e); no headroom factor; FLOAT inputs make these planning values until the certified run
DMIN_RULE = every piece's own threshold dmin is <= the header DH_N<N>_<K>, so P2-12 can cover every pair below the header DH uniformly in J
PLAN_RULE = DH_PLAN_N<N>_<K> is the smallest d from which every input's distance to flip is >= HANDOFF_HR_<K> on every piece (the planning rule); size P2-12 to the larger of DH_PLAN and the certified DH
KINDS = flip same mixed
JOINT_CLASSES = D3 D4 D4M
DH_MAX = 6
HR_LEVELS = 1 1.05 1.1 1.2 1.5 2
